"Shape: Summon": {
  "index": "1",
  "category": "sorcery",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Shape: Summon"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "I can make use of the arcane arts to summon creatures to defend me. \n\nFirst, I will need to fill a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Crystal Phylactery",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " with souls from the creature I want to summon. \n\nThis is done initially by "
        },
        {
          "text": "having the Crystal Phylactery in my offhand when I kill them",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", which sets the Crystal Phylactery to that enemy.  After the first one is set, it just needs to be in my pack to fill the rest of the way.\n\nThen, I hold the spell in one hand, and the phylactery in the other (or wear it on my back). That will determine what I summon. \n\nIt's also worth noting that "
        },
        {
          "text": "any components I put into the spell will be applied to the summon",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", so I should be aware of the implications...and the possibilities."
        },
        {
          "text": "The summon cap by default is 2, with the exception of the ",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " undead, ",
          "color": "dark_gray",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "who gain one additonal additional summon for each tier beyond 2 they attain.",
          "italic": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "related_recipes": [
    {
      "type": "spell_part",
      "location": "mna:shapes/summon"
    },
    {
      "type": "manaweaving_altar",
      "location": "mna:manaweaving/crystal_phylactery"
    }
  ]
}